# Frontend Rules — React 18 + TypeScript 5

## TypeScript Standards
- `strict: true` always — no exceptions
- No `any` — use `unknown` with explicit narrowing if type is truly dynamic
- Import types separately: `import type { Foo } from './types'`
- All component props defined as a `interface Props { ... }` directly above the component
- All API response shapes defined in `src/types/index.ts` — single source of truth

## Component Rules
- Functional components only — no class components
- One component per file, filename matches component name (`GarmentCard.tsx`)
- Max 150 lines per component — extract sub-components or custom hooks if longer
- No business logic inside JSX — extract to hooks or helper functions
- No inline event handlers with complex logic — extract to named handlers

```tsx
// Correct
const handleSave = async () => {
  setSaving(true)
  try { await onSave(form) } finally { setSaving(false) }
}

// Wrong — don't put async logic inline in JSX
<button onClick={async () => { setSaving(true); await onSave(form); setSaving(false) }}>
```

## Hooks Rules
- Custom hooks in `src/hooks/` — prefix with `use`
- Hooks handle: data fetching, polling, state coordination, side effects
- Components only call hooks — they do not call `fetch()` directly
- Cleanup all intervals and subscriptions in useEffect return function

```typescript
// All polling must have cleanup
useEffect(() => {
  load()
  const interval = setInterval(load, POLL_INTERVAL_MS)
  return () => clearInterval(interval)
}, [load])
```

## API Layer
- All `fetch()` calls live in `src/api/garments.ts` only
- Never call `fetch()` inside a component or hook directly
- Always handle non-ok responses: check `res.ok`, parse error body, throw with message
- Type all API functions with explicit return types: `Promise<Garment>`, `Promise<Garment[]>`

```typescript
// Correct API function pattern
export const fetchGarments = async (): Promise<Garment[]> => {
  const res = await fetch('/api/garments')
  if (!res.ok) {
    const body = await res.json().catch(() => ({}))
    throw new Error((body as { error?: string }).error || `HTTP ${res.status}`)
  }
  return res.json()
}
```

## State Management
- Local `useState` for UI state (loading, error, modal open/closed)
- Custom hooks for server state (garment list, polling)
- No Redux, Zustand, or Context API unless the state genuinely needs to cross 3+ component levels
- Optimistic updates: add item to local state immediately, reconcile on next poll

## CSS Rules
- All styles in `src/app.css` using the existing CSS variable system
- New CSS variables go in `:root` at the top of `app.css`
- Class names: BEM-inspired kebab-case (`garment-card__header`, `btn--primary`)
- No inline styles except computed values (e.g., dynamic width for progress bars)
- No `!important` — fix specificity properly

## Accessibility (baseline only — not WCAG AA for MVP)
- All `<button>` elements have visible text or `aria-label`
- All `<img>` elements have descriptive `alt` text
- Form labels must be associated with inputs via `htmlFor` / `id` pairing
- Focus is not trapped or lost when modals open/close

## Performance
- No premature optimisation — add `React.memo` / `useCallback` only with a measured reason
- Images served via MinIO presigned URLs — no base64 data URIs in rendered HTML
- Poll interval is 5000ms minimum — do not reduce without discussing scaling impact
